16:["$","main",null,{"className":"docs_main__7o2m6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_articleMeta__8zYHO","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"MODULE OVERVIEW"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Systems"}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"docs_article__Ja_Vh","children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":[[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Scale and system design"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":["A system design is a set of decisions about how requests move through software, where data lives, what happens under load, and what users see when parts fail. ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Scale"}]," means the system can keep its promised behavior as demand grows. It is not a server count: a fast API with a saturated database or an incorrect cache is not successfully scaled."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":["This module starts with a simple ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"shared document library"}],". A reader opens a document, an editor changes it, and authorized users search their library. We begin with one API process and one database. Each later lesson adds a component only when a stated requirement or measured bottleneck justifies it. The example uses ordinary HTTP and relational data; the principles apply to many products."]}],"\n",["$","figure","p-2",{"className":"docs_studyFigure__4Js_y","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_studyFigureViewport__ZYDNN","children":["$","img","img-0",{"className":"docs_studyFigureImage__Gb2YJ","src":"/learning/scale-design/system-map.svg","alt":"Reader and editor requests enter a service, which reads and writes the primary database and stores document bodies.","width":"920","height":"402","loading":"lazy"}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":"Reader and editor requests enter a service, which reads and writes the primary database and stores document bodies."}]]}],"\n",["$","details","pre-0",{"className":"docs_textDiagram__KfHuf","children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Read the text version of this flow"}],["$","pre",null,{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-aosdf-diagram","children":"Reader / Editor ──▶ API ──▶ Primary database (metadata, access, versions)\n                       └────▶ Object store (document bodies)\n"}]}]]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"id":"who-this-is-for","children":"Who this is for"}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":"Begin with HTTP requests and a database table; no distributed-systems background is assumed. If you already review production architectures, use the worked estimates, failure contracts, and review checklist to challenge your assumptions. Every lesson has a browser-rendered figure, a text alternative, an exercise, and primary references."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"id":"what-you-will-learn","children":"What you will learn"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":"Turn user promises into measurable latency, correctness, capacity, and recovery requirements."}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":"Estimate peak load, concurrency, and p99 latency instead of sizing from average traffic alone."}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":"Place load balancing, gateways, caches, replicas, partitions, and indexes at the right boundary."}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":"Explain exactly what a user may observe during replication lag, simultaneous edits, and network partitions."}],"\n",["$","li","li-4",{"children":"Make API, schema, and operational changes while old and new versions coexist."}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"id":"learning-approach","children":"Learning approach"}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":["Read in order if these topics are new. After each ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Engineering exercise"}],", add a paragraph to one design note for the document library: requirements, capacity estimate, traffic path, cache policy, data access, consistency contract, concurrency rule, and rollout plan. Numbers are illustrative, not universal defaults. A professional design replaces them with measurements and an explicit error budget."]}],"\n","$L22","\n","$L23"],"$L24"]}],"$L25"]}],"$L26"]}]
